<Layout title="Website terms — FetchX"><div class="container legal-page"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">THE TERMS FOR USING THIS WEBSITE</span><h1>Website terms.</h1><p>A clear starting point for exploring FetchX, using a workspace and making an enquiry.</p><span class="legal-date">Effective 2 November 2026</span></div><div class="legal-content"><section><h2>About this website</h2><p>This website is operated by Headrun Technologies Private Limited, India, under the FetchX brand. Contact us at <a href="mailto:karthik@headrun.ai">karthik@headrun.ai</a>. These terms cover use of the marketing website, its illustrative samples, its enquiry form and self-service workspace access.</p></section><section><h2>Enquiries and engagements</h2><p>Sending an enquiry asks us to review your requirements. It is not a purchase, an order acceptance or an agreement to begin work. We qualify your sources and agree scope, deliverables, price and any engagement-specific terms before work starts.</p><p>When self-service is configured, verifying your email creates an account session. You may explicitly create a project, issue working scoped API keys and send requests to destinations approved for that project. Playground requests contact the source and use the project’s configured allocation. Keep keys private and recover uncertain requests using their original operation keys. Source content requires validation by your application; an HTTP success does not establish its accuracy or completeness.</p></section><section><h2>Prices and allowances</h2><p>The USD prices and credit allowances on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> are commercial proposals for review. They become available offers only after the terms, billing implementation and launch are approved. Plan buttons open account signup. They do not purchase, upgrade or activate a plan. The configured service determines trial eligibility and available credits; additional allocation and paid access require explicit approval.</p><p>Complex access, additional sources, increased frequency, API or storage delivery and custom integrations are scoped and quoted before work begins. Applicable taxes and any additional charges will be stated in the agreed quote. Website information may change; the accepted engagement documents govern your purchase.</p></section><section><h2>Coverage and examples</h2><p>Source coverage is subject to qualification. We do not promise access to every website, universal CAPTCHA resolution, a particular success rate or an unagreed delivery schedule.</p><p>The downloadable sample datasets are fictional and illustrative, not live feeds or records of actual products, properties or shipments. You may use them to evaluate formats and prototype an integration. Do not rely on them for operational, financial or other real-world decisions. Developer requests use placeholders; access to a customer endpoint must be provisioned separately.</p></section><section><h2>Responsible use</h2><p>Please provide accurate contact and scoping information. Do not submit passwords, tokens, sensitive personal information or material you are not authorised to share. Do not attempt to disrupt the website, evade its form protections or gain unauthorised access to information or systems.</p><p>Submitting a source URL in an enquiry does not cause it to be fetched. Sending a playground request explicitly asks the gateway to contact that source within the project’s approved access. Neither action establishes that the source can be collected or accepted for your use. Access rights, lawful use and relevant data requirements must be assessed as part of qualification.</p></section><section><h2>Website materials and external links</h2><p>FetchX branding, website design and original content belong to Headrun Technologies Private Limited or their respective owners. The FetchX source repository is governed by the licence stated in that repository. External websites are operated by their own providers and have their own terms.</p></section><section><h2>Availability and responsibility</h2><p>We aim to keep the website accurate and available, but it may contain errors or be temporarily unavailable. Website information is provided for general evaluation and does not replace an agreed scope or contract. Nothing in these terms excludes a responsibility or right that applicable law does not permit to be excluded.</p><p>For account and enquiry-data handling, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a>. We may update these website terms by publishing a revised version with a new effective date. Separate written terms govern any paid engagement.</p></section></div></div></Layout>
